diff --git a/docs/HTTP API.md b/docs/HTTP API.md
index 11fc55e..f6d3548 100644
--- a/docs/HTTP API.md	
+++ b/docs/HTTP API.md	
@@ -76,7 +76,9 @@ Some functionality is exposed as RPC-style calls
 * `GET /.ping`: Returns 200 with body `OK` if the server is available.
 * `POST /.shell`: Run a shell command on the server side and return the result.
 * `POST /.logs`: Accepts a JSON array of log entry objects with fields `source`, `level`, `message`, and `timestamp`. The server logs these with the client's IP. Returns `OK`.
-* `* /.proxy/<host[:port]>/path`: Proxy an HTTP request to avoid CORS issues.
+* `OPTIONS /.proxy/`: Authenticated capability probe. Returns 204 with `x-silverbullet-proxy-version: 2` when explicit HTTP(S) targets are supported. Disabled in read-only mode. No outbound request is made.
+* `* /.proxy/<percent-encoded absolute HTTP(S) URL>`: Proxy a request while preserving its explicit scheme, host, path and query. URLs containing credentials are rejected; tunnel an `Authorization` header instead. For example, encode the entire `https://localhost:8443/v1?key=value` URL as a single path component.
+* `* /.proxy/<host[:port]>/path`: Legacy proxy form to avoid CORS issues.
   * Blocked in read-only mode (returns 405).
   * The URI does not include a scheme — it is auto-detected: `http://` is used for `localhost`, `127.0.0.1`, bare IP addresses, and `host.docker.internal`; `https://` is used for everything else.
   * Request headers prefixed with `X-Proxy-Header-` have the prefix stripped and are forwarded to the upstream server.
